# AGENTS.md

This file provides guidance to AI coding agents working in this repository.

This is a Ruby on Rails <%= Rails::VERSION::MAJOR %>.<%= Rails::VERSION::MINOR %> application<% if options[:api] %> configured as an API-only app<% end %>.
Follow Rails conventions: prefer what the framework provides over adding new
dependencies or custom abstractions.

## Setup

```bash
bin/setup                # Install dependencies<% unless options.skip_active_record? %> and prepare the database<% end %>
<% if options[:api] -%>
bin/rails server         # Start the server
<% else -%>
bin/dev                  # Start the development server
<% end -%>
```

## Commands

```bash
<% unless options[:skip_test] -%>
bin/rails test           # Run the test suite
bin/rails test test/models/user_test.rb:12   # Run a single test
<% if depends_on_system_test? -%>
bin/rails test:system    # Run system tests
<% end -%>
<% end -%>
<% unless options.skip_rubocop? -%>
bin/rubocop              # Lint Ruby code (add -a to autocorrect)
<% end -%>
<% unless options.skip_brakeman? -%>
bin/brakeman             # Static security analysis
<% end -%>
<% unless options.skip_bundler_audit? -%>
bin/bundler-audit        # Audit gems for known vulnerabilities
<% end -%>
bin/ci                   # Run every check from config/ci.rb, as CI does
bin/rails generate --help   # List available generators
```

Run `bin/ci` before considering a change complete.

## Conventions

- Application code lives in `app/`, configuration in `config/`<% unless options[:skip_test] %>, and tests in `test/` (Minitest, not RSpec)<% end %>.
<% unless options.skip_active_record? -%>
- Change the database schema through migrations (`bin/rails generate migration`), never by editing `db/schema.rb` directly.
<% end -%>
- Use generators (`bin/rails generate`) for new models, controllers, and other components so files land in the expected places.
<% unless options[:skip_test] -%>
- Add or update tests alongside every behavior change.
<% end -%>
- Store secrets in encrypted credentials (`bin/rails credentials:edit`), never in source control.
<% if using_importmap? -%>
- JavaScript dependencies are managed with importmap (`bin/importmap pin <package>`), not npm.
<% elsif using_bun? -%>
- JavaScript dependencies are managed with Bun (`bun add <package>`).
<% elsif using_node? -%>
- JavaScript dependencies are managed with Yarn (`yarn add <package>`).
<% end -%>
